[Opening "Semi-Slav Defense: Meran Variation, Blumenfeld Variation"]

{Semi-Slav Defense: Meran Variation, Blumenfeld Variation. A slight inaccuracy in move order — the bishop is better placed before this pawn commits.}
1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 d5 4. Nc3 c6 5. e3 Nbd7 {Book so far. The plan is the usual one: finish development, then decide which side to open.} 6. Bd3 dxc4 7. Bxc4 b5 8. Bd3 ! a6 {Here the exchange is tempting and wrong: trading the good bishop leaves the dark squares bare.} (8... b4 Rb1 b3 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. e4 c5 10. e5 cxd4 11. Nxb5 axb5 ?! 12. exf6 gxf6 13. O-O Qb6 14. Qe2 b4 15. Bf4 Bc5 16. Nd2 Bb7 17. a4 e5 18. Ne4 Rg8 19. a5 Qe6 20. Bg3 Be7 21. a6 Bd5 22. a7 f5 23. Ra6 Nb6 24. Nd2 Kf8 25. Bxf5 Qxf5 26. Rxb6 Rxa7 27. Rb8+ Kg7 28. Bxe5+ f6 29. Bxd4 Rd7 30. Rxg8+ Kxg8 31. Ra1 h5 32. Be3 Qg6 33. f3 Qc2 34. Qb5 Bc6 35. Qc4+ Qxc4 36. Nxc4 Kf7 37. Ra5 Rd5 38. Ra7 Rd7 39. Ra5 Rd5 40. Ra7 Rd7 {The rest is technique, which is another way of saying it still has to be played accurately.} 41. Ra5 1/2-1/2

