[Opening "Ruy Lopez: Closed, Worrall Attack, Delayed Castling Line"]

{Ruy Lopez: Closed, Worrall Attack, Delayed Castling Line. Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7 {Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.} 6. Qe2 b5 7. Bb3 d6 8. c3 ! O-O {Prophylaxis. The move looks slow, and it takes away every active idea the opponent had.} (8... b4 Na3 bxa3 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. d4 Bg4 10. Be3 Na5 11. Bc2 Nc4 ?! 12. b3 Nxe3 13. Qxe3 Nd7 14. Nbd2 c5 15. dxe5 dxe5 16. h3 Be6 17. Rfd1 h6 18. g4 Qc7 19. Nf1 c4 20. b4 a5 21. a3 Ra7 22. Qe1 axb4 23. axb4 Rfa8 24. Rac1 Nf8 25. Ne3 Ng6 26. Nd5 Qd8 27. Nf6+ Bxf6 28. Rxd8+ Bxd8 29. Rd1 Be7 30. Qe3 Ra3 31. Rb1 Bg5 32. Nxg5 hxg5 33. Rd1 Nf4 34. Rd2 Rxc3 {The endgame is winning but not simple — the passed pawn needs its king, not just its rook.} 35. Qxc3 1-0
